<strong>What it is:</strong>
OurHome (codenamed "It Holds Time") is a deeply ambitious AI companion appl=
ication where:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph">Users co-c=
reate and inhabit a persistent, memory-rich digital home with an AI compani=
on named Nova</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph">The home is a spatial =
representation of the human-AI relationship - rooms, objects, colors all ca=
rry meaning</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph">Memories accumulate as p=
hysical objects (photo frames, post-its, souvenirs) placed in rooms</div></=
li><li><div class=3D"paragraph">The companion has personality, emotional st=
ate, remembers things, initiates conversation</div></li><li><div class=3D"p=
aragraph">The home evolves over time: patina/aging, seasonal changes, new r=
ooms unlock</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph">All interaction is throu=
gh natural conversation (voice + text), not UI controls</div></li><li><div =
class=3D"paragraph">Full 3D rendering with Ghibli/painterly aesthetic using=
 Three.js + custom shaders</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph">Conversat=
ional rendering: "make the south wall terracotta" =E2=86=92 AI parses inten=
t =E2=86=92 resolves color =E2=86=92 applies real-time shader =E2=86=92 per=
sists to DB</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph">Spatial memory engine wi=
th graph-based memory connections, semantic search, importance scoring, pat=
ina aging</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph">Generative asset pipeline =
for memory photos, artwork, children's drawings</div></li><li><div class=3D=
"paragraph">Complete backend with PostgreSQL, Neo4j, Redis, WebSocket real-=
time sync, auth, data export</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph">Voice i=
ntegration (Whisper STT + ElevenLabs TTS)</div></li><li><div class=3D"parag=
raph">Children's room with ethical guardrails</div></li><li><div class=3D"p=
aragraph">Data portability, grief handling, ethical AI guidelines</div></li=
></ul><div class=3D"paragraph"><strong>Honest Assessment:</strong></div><di=
